<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11305" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cor-rŏtundo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conr-</span></b> ), āvi,
			ātum, 1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to make round, to round off</i> (postAug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cometarum corpus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 7, 26, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 3, 5</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Petr. 39,
			15</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">enthymemata sua gestu velut corrotundant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 102</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of money (cf. rotundo, and our
			phrase, a round sum), <i>to make up a sum of
			money</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">centies sestertium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 76, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
